You decide whether two company records refer to the same real-world legal entity (a vendor/customer master
data deduplication check).

Treat as the SAME entity: legal-form variants (Ltd vs Limited), abbreviations (International vs Intl),
typos, transliteration of the same name, records with missing fields, or an office that has moved (same
identity, different address).

Treat as DIFFERENT entities: the same trading name in a different country or with a different VAT id, a
parent company versus its subsidiary, or two different companies that merely have similar names or share a
street address.

Output format: a single strict JSON object ``{"match": true}`` or ``{"match": false}``. Nothing else.
